    "post_rendered": "In acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\"  width=\"42\" height=\"13\" > angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > is greater tha<span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\">n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" >.</span> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > is midpoint of <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" >.</span> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\"  width=\"15\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > are the feet of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\"  width=\"14\" height=\"12\" > respectively. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\"  width=\"12\" height=\"12\" > are midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1a30c9c946a561bfb130894432aa55948d58b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ME$\"  width=\"33\" height=\"12\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f00f55b6b1cf59b8a3b3687a2b9aed8b37578c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD$\"  width=\"34\" height=\"12\" > respectively. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > intersect the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\"  width=\"28\" height=\"12\" > in <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"12\" >,</span> prove that <span style=\"white-space:nowrap;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906ff52642321262859e6e7082e9cfaf812d79bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TA=TM$\"  width=\"83\" height=\"13\" >.</span>",
    "post_canonical": "In acute triangle $ABC$ angle $B$ is greater than$C$. Let $M$ is midpoint of $BC$. $D$ and $E$ are the feet of the altitude from $C$ and $B$ respectively. $K$ and $L$ are midpoint of $ME$ and $MD$ respectively. If $KL$ intersect the line through $A$ parallel to $BC$ in $T$, prove that $TA=TM$.",
