   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 2266399,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 405943,
    "poster_id": 91362,
    "post_rendered": "Define a finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"13\" > to be 'good' if it satisfies the following conditions:<br>\n\n<ul class=\"bbcode_list\">\n<li><b>(a)</b> For every three disjoint element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1e22fe09c7388d738ebd1e52fb999e0eae620f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" > like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" > we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d19cb6340607316745cc7eb977af6b74a9475c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(a,b,c)=1;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" ><br>\n</li>\n<li><b>(b)</b> For every two distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e157e676b4f5709794247599f06f4460e81bf84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,c\\in A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" > there exists an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c81dc3553171ffd414b2a9b0f320b17a19cc581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" > distinct from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9dd1fe4590b39259c898e9d691785862c2ce836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"16\" > such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe207dd510fa3e2012d9747d93de6f9cc71bf3f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bc$\"  width=\"16\" height=\"12\" > is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\"  width=\"13\" height=\"8\" ></li>\n</ul>\n<br>\nFind all good sets.",
    "post_canonical": "Define a finite set $A$ to be 'good' if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n[list][*][b](a)[/b] For every three disjoint element of $A,$ like $a,b,c$ we have $\\gcd(a,b,c)=1;$\n\n[*][b](b)[/b] For every two distinct $b,c\\in A,$ there exists an $a\\in A,$ distinct from $b,c$ such that $bc$ is divisible by $a.$[/list]\n\nFind all good sets.",
